# ORIGINS architecture guardrails

Follow `docs/GAME_ARCHITECTURE_V1.md` as the canonical layout.

## Folder ownership
- Browser executable code: `apps/web/`
- Reusable game primitives: `packages/game-core/`
- Room/cell/collision/door engine: `packages/map-engine/`
- Dungeon progression and encounter flow: `packages/gameplay/`
- Declarative manifests/data: `packages/content/`
- Rendering adapters: `packages/rendering/`
- Generic shared helpers only: `packages/shared/`
- Approved runtime assets: `assets/game/`
- Source/provenance assets: `assets/source/`
- Existing map research recipes: `origins/map-engine/` — preserve
- Crystal extraction tools: `tools/crystal-map-importer/` — preserve

## Boundaries
- Do not put core game rules inside React/UI components.
- Do not put DOM/browser-specific code in `game-core` or pure map data modules.
- Do not hardcode dungeon asset paths throughout gameplay logic; use manifests.
- Do not create a second map engine in another folder.
- Do not import source-analysis tools into runtime code.

## Current milestone scope
Only build the web shell, map engine skeleton, `zuma_gray` runtime theme, Standard Room, KingRoom, collision and door-state preview.
Do not add player systems, monsters, combat, spells, inventory, networking or unrelated UI yet.
